      "side": 1,
      "message": "Both `SendBootromCommandSha` and `SendBootromCommandAes` contain identical, verbose logic to read the inner payload length from the response buffer, calculate the safe payload boundary, and protect against out-of-bounds reads. Extracting this into a single helper method removes duplicate code and centralizes boundary validation.\n\n### Detailed Fix\n\n**Location:** `util/egis/bootrom.h` (Declaration) and `util/egis/bootrom.cc` (Implementation)\n\nDeclare the private helper in `BootromComm`:\n\n```c\n  std::expected\u003cstd::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e, BootromError\u003e ExtractWrappedPayload(\n      std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e response, size_t header_size);\n\n```\n\nImplement it:\n\n```c\nstd::expected\u003cstd::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e, BootromError\u003e\nBootromComm::ExtractWrappedPayload(std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e response,\n                                   size_t header_size) {\n  auto len_res \u003d\n      ReadLittleEndian\u003cuint32_t\u003e(response.subspan(kStatusHeaderSize));\n  if (!len_res) return std::unexpected(BootromError::kResponseTruncated);\n\n  uint32_t rsp_wrapped_len \u003d std::min\u003cuint32_t\u003e(\n      len_res.value(), response.size() - header_size);\n\n  return response.subspan(header_size, rsp_wrapped_len);\n}\n\n```\n\nUpdate `SendBootromCommandSha`:\n\n```c\n  // ... (send logic) ...\n  auto ret_res \u003d DoUsbTransfer(cmd, kScHeaderSizeSha, timeout);\n  if (!ret_res) return std::unexpected(ret_res.error());\n\n  auto payload_res \u003d ExtractWrappedPayload(ret_res.value(), kScHeaderSizeSha);\n  if (!payload_res) return std::unexpected(payload_res.error());\n\n  return std::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e(payload_res-\u003ebegin(), payload_res-\u003eend());\n\n```\n\nUpdate `SendBootromCommandAes`:\n\n```c\n  // ... (send logic) ...\n  auto ret_res \u003d DoUsbTransfer(cmd, kScHeaderSizeAes, timeout);\n  if (!ret_res) return std::unexpected(ret_res.error());\n  \n  auto payload_res \u003d ExtractWrappedPayload(ret_res.value(), kScHeaderSizeAes);\n  if (!payload_res) return std::unexpected(payload_res.error());\n\n  // Extract IV and Tag dynamically from the response buffer\n  size_t offset \u003d kStatusHeaderSize + kWrappedCommandSize;\n  auto rsp_iv \u003d std::span(ret_res.value()).subspan(offset, kAesGcmIvSize);\n  offset +\u003d kAesGcmIvSize;\n  auto rsp_tag \u003d std::span(ret_res.value()).subspan(offset, kAesGcmTagSize);\n  \n  std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e rsp_payload \u003d payload_res.value();\n  std::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e decrypted_payload(rsp_payload.size());\n\n  if (!AesGcmDecryptOpenssl(aes_key_, rsp_iv, aad, rsp_payload, rsp_tag,\n                            decrypted_payload)) {\n    std::println(stderr, \"[ERROR] AES-GCM Authentication Failed (Tag mismatch)\");\n    return std::unexpected(BootromError::kGcmAuthenticationFailed);\n  }\n\n  return decrypted_payload;\n\n```",
