      "message": "**Location:** `util/egis/bootrom.cc` (`GetBootromInfo` and `GetFlashInfo`)\n\n**The Problem:** You are passing magic numbers like `12` and `40` as expected response sizes, and using manual offsets (`payload.subspan(4)`, `resp-\u003edata() + 8`) to extract data.\n\n**The Fix:** Define packed structs in `bootrom.h` to represent these response payloads. This eliminates the magic numbers, documents the protocol, and makes extraction robust.\n\n*In `bootrom.h`:*\n\n```c\nnamespace EgisBootrom {\n// ... existing constants ...\n\nstruct BootromInfoResponse {\n  uint32_t version;\n  uint32_t max_cmd_size;\n  uint32_t max_fw_upgrade_size;\n} __attribute__((packed));\n\nstruct FlashInfoResponse {\n  uint32_t flash_size;\n  uint32_t reserved; \n  char prod_name[8];\n  // Note: The rest of the 40-byte payload can be mapped here or left implicit\n} __attribute__((packed));\n\n} // namespace EgisBootrom\n\n```\n\n*In `bootrom.cc`:*\n\n```c\nstd::expected\u003cvoid, BootromError\u003e BootromComm::GetBootromInfo() {\n  std::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e cmd \u003d {EgisBootrom::kCmdGetBootInfo};\n  \n  // Use sizeof() instead of 12\n  auto resp \u003d SendBootromCommand(cmd, sizeof(EgisBootrom::BootromInfoResponse));\n  if (!resp) return std::unexpected(resp.error());\n\n  if (resp-\u003esize() \u003e\u003d sizeof(EgisBootrom::BootromInfoResponse)) {\n    const auto* info \u003d reinterpret_cast\u003cconst EgisBootrom::BootromInfoResponse*\u003e(resp-\u003edata());\n    \n    // Use FromLittleEndian from the earlier refactor!\n    std::println(\"Bootrom Version: 0x{:x}\", FromLittleEndian(info-\u003eversion));\n    std::println(\"Max Command Size: {} bytes\", FromLittleEndian(info-\u003emax_cmd_size));\n    std::println(\"Max FW Upgrade Size: {} bytes\", FromLittleEndian(info-\u003emax_fw_upgrade_size));\n  }\n  return {};\n}\n\n```\n\n*(Apply the exact same struct-casting pattern to `GetFlashInfo` to get rid of `resp-\u003edata() + 8`.)*",
