      "message": "**Location:** `util/egis/et171_flash.cc` (`GetNextPacketSize`)\n\n**The Problem:** When parsing the wrapped packet headers, you have:\n\n```c\nauto wrapped_size \u003d ReadLittleEndian\u003cuint32_t\u003e(fw.subspan(2, 4));\n\n```\n\n`2` and `4` are magic numbers representing the offset and size of the `payload_len` field. If the header ever changes, this breaks silently.\n\n**The Fix:** Since you already defined `SecureCommandShaHeader` at the top of the file, use `offsetof` and `sizeof` to make it strictly tied to the struct definition.\n\n```c\n  auto wrapped_size \u003d ReadLittleEndian\u003cuint32_t\u003e(\n      fw.subspan(offsetof(SecureCommandShaHeader, payload_len), \n                 sizeof(SecureCommandShaHeader::payload_len)));\n\n```",
